{"summary":"Restore surrounding-whitespace parsing and reject duplicated signs in SimpleAtof and SimpleAtod.","explanation":"NumbersTest.Atod expects SimpleAtod("  3.141  ", &d) to return true, but it returns false because only leading ASCII whitespace is stripped and from_chars must consume the remaining input. NumbersTest.Prefixes expects SimpleAtod("+-1", &d) and SimpleAtof("+-1", &f) to return false, but both return true because the parsers skip '+' and then accept '-1'. Strip ASCII whitespace at both ends and reject another sign immediately after the skipped '+'.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/numbers.cc","old":"bool SimpleAtof(absl::string_view str, float* absl_nonnull out) {
  *out = 0.0;
  str = StripLeadingAsciiWhitespace(str);
  if (str.empty()) {
    // absl::from_chars doesn't accept empty strings.
    return false;
  }
  // std::from_chars doesn't accept an initial +, but SimpleAtof does, so if one
  // is present, skip it, while avoiding accepting "+-0" as valid.
  if (str[0] == '+') {
    str.remove_prefix(1);
    if (str.empty()) {
      return false;
    }
  }","new":"bool SimpleAtof(absl::string_view str, float* absl_nonnull out) {
  *out = 0.0;
  str = StripAsciiWhitespace(str);
  if (str.empty()) {
    // absl::from_chars doesn't accept empty strings.
    return false;
  }
  // std::from_chars doesn't accept an initial +, but SimpleAtof does, so if one
  // is present, skip it, while avoiding accepting "+-0" as valid.
  if (str[0] == '+') {
    str.remove_prefix(1);
    if (str.empty() || str[0] == '+' || str[0] == '-') {
      return false;
    }
  }"},{"path":"absl/strings/numbers.cc","old":"bool SimpleAtod(absl::string_view str, double* absl_nonnull out) {
  *out = 0.0;
  str = StripLeadingAsciiWhitespace(str);
  if (str.empty()) {
    // absl::from_chars doesn't accept empty strings.
    return false;
  }
  // std::from_chars doesn't accept an initial +, but SimpleAtod does, so if one
  // is present, skip it, while avoiding accepting "+-0" as valid.
  if (str[0] == '+') {
    str.remove_prefix(1);
    if (str.empty()) {
      return false;
    }
  }","new":"bool SimpleAtod(absl::string_view str, double* absl_nonnull out) {
  *out = 0.0;
  str = StripAsciiWhitespace(str);
  if (str.empty()) {
    // absl::from_chars doesn't accept empty strings.
    return false;
  }
  // std::from_chars doesn't accept an initial +, but SimpleAtod does, so if one
  // is present, skip it, while avoiding accepting "+-0" as valid.
  if (str[0] == '+') {
    str.remove_prefix(1);
    if (str.empty() || str[0] == '+' || str[0] == '-') {
      return false;
    }
  }"}]}
